// Probe 83 — Cluster I sequence: back-to-back `??` Sets
//
// `a = vec[i] ?? "x"; b = vec[j] ?? "y";` — two sequential `??` Sets.
// Each Set allocates its own `_ncc_N`.  Does the second Set's `_ncc_N+1`
// land in the slot the first one freed (slot recycling)?  And does the
// scope-exit free ordering interact in any surprising way?
//
// Pairing: 02 (single ??), 37 (tuple destructure of two ??s).
// Status: cluster I sequencing probe.

struct H { items: vector<text> }

